<title>UK: UK output prices rise 0.2 pct in April.</title>
<headline>UK output prices rise 0.2 pct in April.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in April (previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    OUTPUT PRICES (unadj) APRIL    MARCH (PREL MARCH)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.2	-0.1    (-0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    0.8	1.0     (1.0)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     125.0    124.8   (124.8)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.1	0.2     (0.2)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    0.5	0.5     (0.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     120.7    120.6   (120.6)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD,DRINK,TOBACCO,PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.1	0.2     (0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	    0.5	0.5     (O.5)</p>
<p>    Qtr/qtr change	  0.1	unch     (0.1)</p>
<p>    Qtr/Qtr annual rate   0.3	0.1     (0.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     120.4    120.3   (120.3)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  -2.1     -1.3    (-0.9)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    -10.5    -8.0    (-7.6)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     104.3    106.5   (106.9)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -1.9     -0.8    (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	   -10.5    -8.2    (-7.7)</p>
<p>    Index		     104.0   106.0   (106.6)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F,D,T,P (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -1.4     -1.1    (-0.7)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	   -8.2     -7.1    (-6.7)</p>
<p>    Index		     102.2   103.6   (104.0)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F,D,T,P (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -1.2	unch    (0.4)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr  change	  -8.2	-7.2    (-6.6)</p>
<p>    Index		     102.5    103.7   (104.3)</p>
<p>    INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE    APRIL M/M    APRIL Y/Y</p>
<p>    fuel				    -3.6	  -4.4</p>
<p>    crude oil etc			 -12.8	 -25.0</p>
<p>    food (home produced)		-0.1	  -11.7</p>
<p>    food (imported)			1.2	   -3.4</p>
<p>    metals				  -1.4	  -11.5</p>
<p>    chemicals			     -0.4	  -9.4</p>
<p>    other home produced		  1.4	   -0.7</p>
<p>    Other imported materials	  -1.2	   -9.2</p>
<p>Consensus of economists' forecasts was for input prices to fall a seasonally adjusted 0.5 percent and fall 8.4 percent year-on-year. Output prices forecast +0.1 on the month, +0.8 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>The ONS said the rise in output prices of 0.8 percent in the year to April was the lowest rate of increase since September 1986. Prices of petroleum products have fallen by 5.1 percent since December.</p>
<p>The 10.5 percent drop in input prices was the largest annual fall since November 1986.</p>
<p>Input prices excluding food, beverages, tobacco and petroleum fell by 8.2 percent in the year to April, the largest annual fall since August 1986.</p>
